WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.440
Welcome to the Claude Certified Architect Foundations course.

2
00:00:03.440 --> 00:00:04.559
I'm glad you're here.

3
00:00:04.559 --> 00:00:07.480
Before we start, I want to cover what the exam is,

4
00:00:07.480 --> 00:00:10.880
who it's for, and how to get the most out of this course.

5
00:00:10.880 --> 00:00:13.760
The exam is 60 questions in two hours,

6
00:00:13.760 --> 00:00:17.059
and you need a scaled score of 720 out of 1,000.

7
00:00:17.059 --> 00:00:20.200
It's a proctored exam online or at a test center,

8
00:00:20.200 --> 00:00:24.040
and the fee is $125 at the time of this recording.

9
00:00:24.040 --> 00:00:26.159
The content spans five domains.

10
00:00:26.159 --> 00:00:28.319
Agentic architectures and orchestration

11
00:00:28.319 --> 00:00:32.240
is the heaviest at 27%, then Claude code configuration

12
00:00:32.240 --> 00:00:34.680
and prompt engineering at 20% each,

13
00:00:34.680 --> 00:00:37.880
tool design and MCP integration at 18%,

14
00:00:37.880 --> 00:00:40.159
and context management and reliability

15
00:00:40.159 --> 00:00:44.759
at 15%, which in my opinion, is the most important domain.

16
00:00:44.759 --> 00:00:46.659
Anthropic recommends around six months

17
00:00:46.659 --> 00:00:50.360
of hands-on work with the Claude APIs, the agent SDK,

18
00:00:50.360 --> 00:00:54.560
Claude code, and MCP before you sit for this exam.

19
00:00:54.680 --> 00:00:56.360
One more thing before the lessons start

20
00:00:56.360 --> 00:00:59.080
because it changes how you move through the course.

21
00:00:59.080 --> 00:01:02.560
This program comes with a custom study pack.

22
00:01:02.560 --> 00:01:04.400
It's far more than a simple handout.

23
00:01:04.400 --> 00:01:06.800
There's a study companion that condenses the whole course

24
00:01:06.800 --> 00:01:09.900
into one document, a 30-day study plan

25
00:01:09.900 --> 00:01:12.599
that names the exact lectures to watch each day

26
00:01:12.599 --> 00:01:14.680
to be certified in a month,

27
00:01:14.680 --> 00:01:18.480
and three free mini-exam assessments at 30 questions each,

28
00:01:18.480 --> 00:01:21.400
all with full question and answer explanations.

29
00:01:21.400 --> 00:01:24.879
It also has a key terms glossary, printable flashcards,

30
00:01:24.879 --> 00:01:28.500
and every slide deck from this course for you to use.

31
00:01:28.500 --> 00:01:31.559
It doesn't cost a thing and it stays up to date.

32
00:01:31.559 --> 00:01:33.519
The last video in this course

33
00:01:33.519 --> 00:01:35.400
shows you exactly how to get it.

34
00:01:35.400 --> 00:01:38.400
It's free and it takes less than a minute to download.

35
00:01:38.400 --> 00:01:40.360
I'd go get it before starting the lessons

36
00:01:40.360 --> 00:01:42.800
because the study pack is what turns this course

37
00:01:42.800 --> 00:01:47.239
into a concrete path to success on exam day.

38
00:01:47.239 --> 00:01:49.199
In fact, let's quickly walk through

39
00:01:49.199 --> 00:01:51.080
how to download the resources.

40
00:01:51.760 --> 00:01:54.480
First, scroll all the way to the last lesson of the course

41
00:01:54.480 --> 00:01:56.800
and click on the Resources button.

42
00:01:56.800 --> 00:01:58.480
You'll need to scroll down a little bit more,

43
00:01:58.480 --> 00:02:00.680
then click the provided link.

44
00:02:00.680 --> 00:02:03.160
Once on the site, enter your information,

45
00:02:03.160 --> 00:02:05.800
then verify your account and it will redirect you

46
00:02:05.800 --> 00:02:08.080
to all the available resources.

47
00:02:08.080 --> 00:02:10.520
Look, people have different learning styles.

48
00:02:10.520 --> 00:02:13.600
Some really like using the slide decks and the study plan,

49
00:02:13.600 --> 00:02:15.440
along with the other resources.

50
00:02:15.440 --> 00:02:18.380
If that's you, pause here and go get them.

51
00:02:18.380 --> 00:02:20.880
If you're the type that doesn't need all that extra stuff,

52
00:02:21.639 --> 00:02:22.479
don't worry about it.

53
00:02:22.479 --> 00:02:24.240
Thousands of students have passed

54
00:02:24.240 --> 00:02:26.520
using only the video materials.

55
00:02:26.520 --> 00:02:28.320
That's actually how I like to learn.

56
00:02:29.460 --> 00:02:30.960
Now that you know about the study pack,

57
00:02:30.960 --> 00:02:33.119
we should talk about who this course is for

58
00:02:33.119 --> 00:02:36.500
because I'd rather you find out now than three lessons in.

59
00:02:36.500 --> 00:02:39.539
This course assumes you already use Cloud for real work.

60
00:02:39.539 --> 00:02:43.080
I don't cover setup and I don't walk through configuration.

61
00:02:43.080 --> 00:02:45.880
I also don't run code on screen.

62
00:02:45.880 --> 00:02:47.160
When I mention an example,

63
00:02:47.160 --> 00:02:50.000
I'm assuming you could go rebuild it on your own

64
00:02:50.000 --> 00:02:52.759
in your environment without me talking you through it.

65
00:02:52.759 --> 00:02:56.119
If that isn't where you are yet, that's completely fine.

66
00:02:56.119 --> 00:02:58.440
But this isn't your starting point.

67
00:02:58.440 --> 00:03:00.399
Go find a more foundational course

68
00:03:00.399 --> 00:03:02.600
and get some hands-on hours first.

69
00:03:02.600 --> 00:03:04.520
This course will be here when you're ready

70
00:03:04.520 --> 00:03:07.220
and you'll get far more out of it after doing that.

71
00:03:08.779 --> 00:03:10.600
Here's something that surprises people.

72
00:03:10.600 --> 00:03:14.360
This credential is valid for 12 months and then it expires.

73
00:03:14.360 --> 00:03:15.479
That isn't a catch.

74
00:03:15.479 --> 00:03:18.679
It's an honest response to a moving target.

75
00:03:18.679 --> 00:03:21.440
Cloud changes fast and a credential that stayed valid

76
00:03:21.440 --> 00:03:23.380
for five years would end up certifying

77
00:03:23.380 --> 00:03:25.320
that you knew a version of old Cloud

78
00:03:25.320 --> 00:03:27.520
that isn't valid anymore.

79
00:03:27.520 --> 00:03:30.059
So Anthropic keeps it current instead.

80
00:03:30.059 --> 00:03:31.720
When your renewal window opens,

81
00:03:31.720 --> 00:03:35.000
you renew what changed since you last certified.

82
00:03:35.000 --> 00:03:37.759
And it's completely free and non-proctored.

83
00:03:37.759 --> 00:03:41.279
The assessment is on the Anthropic Partner Academy website.

84
00:03:41.279 --> 00:03:43.960
There's no fee when you renew on time.

85
00:03:43.960 --> 00:03:46.039
What that buys you is a current tense statement

86
00:03:46.039 --> 00:03:48.520
that you know today's Cloud.

87
00:03:49.240 --> 00:03:50.279
And that you're an expert in Cloud

88
00:03:50.279 --> 00:03:52.539
as it stands in the current tense.

89
00:03:53.880 --> 00:03:55.500
There are two ways through this course,

90
00:03:55.500 --> 00:03:57.279
depending on where you are.

91
00:03:57.279 --> 00:03:58.940
If you're preparing for the first time,

92
00:03:58.940 --> 00:04:00.360
watch the lessons in order.

93
00:04:00.360 --> 00:04:01.559
They build on each other.

94
00:04:01.559 --> 00:04:05.419
So resist the urge to skip ahead on your first pass.

95
00:04:05.419 --> 00:04:07.740
Then work through the practice exams

96
00:04:07.740 --> 00:04:09.059
until you're scoring comfortably

97
00:04:09.059 --> 00:04:11.740
above that passing line of 720.

98
00:04:11.740 --> 00:04:13.160
If you're coming back to renew,

99
00:04:13.160 --> 00:04:15.059
you don't need to rewatch everything.

100
00:04:15.059 --> 00:04:16.600
Start with what changed.

101
00:04:16.600 --> 00:04:19.559
Watch the updated lessons and run fresh practice questions

102
00:04:19.559 --> 00:04:21.959
to confirm your judgment still tracks.

103
00:04:21.959 --> 00:04:25.480
Either way, the practice exams are your calibration tool.

104
00:04:25.480 --> 00:04:27.559
And there are plenty of them right here,

105
00:04:27.559 --> 00:04:29.399
all in one platform.

106
00:04:29.399 --> 00:04:31.519
Your access includes every update.

107
00:04:31.519 --> 00:04:34.480
So what you come back to is always current.

108
00:04:36.079 --> 00:04:37.399
One last piece of advice,

109
00:04:37.399 --> 00:04:40.320
and it's the one that pays off every renewal cycle.

110
00:04:40.320 --> 00:04:42.880
Learn the patterns, not the signatures.

111
00:04:42.880 --> 00:04:46.320
Names change, parameters change, and limits change.

112
00:04:47.040 --> 00:04:49.320
The reasoning behind a good design decision is durable.

113
00:04:49.320 --> 00:04:52.959
And that reasoning is what the exam is actually testing.

114
00:04:52.959 --> 00:04:55.059
When something is stable, I'll tell you.

115
00:04:55.059 --> 00:04:57.880
And when something is volatile, I'll tell you that too.

116
00:04:57.880 --> 00:05:00.859
So you know where your study time is worth spending.

117
00:05:00.859 --> 00:05:02.679
All right, that's enough talk.

118
00:05:02.679 --> 00:05:04.040
Let's get into the content.

